  * With `vTaskDelay()`, the period between successive executions includes the delay period *plus* the time the task spent executing and any time it was preempted by higher-priority tasks. This causes the execution frequency to drift over time.
  * With `vTaskDelayUntil()`, the parameter `pxPreviousWakeTime` is automatically updated internally to track the scheduled wake-up tick count [FreeRTOS_Ref_Manual p.40–41]. It automatically compensates for the execution duration of the task, preventing timing drift.

