```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void tim3_ch1_pwm_init(void)
{
    /* 1. Enable GPIOA and TIM3 peripheral clocks */
    RCC->AHB2ENR  |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN;
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_TIM3EN;

    /* 2. Configure PA6 as Alternate Function 2 (TIM3_CH1), high speed */
    GPIOA->MODER   = (GPIOA->MODER & ~GPIO_MODER_MODE6_Msk) 
                   | (0x2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE6_Pos);            /* AF mode (10b) */
    GPIOA->AFR[0]  = (GPIOA->AFR[0] & ~GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL6_Msk) 
                   | (2U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL6_Pos);              /* AF2 */
    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (0x3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED6_Pos);       /* Very high speed */

    /* 3. Configure TIM3 time base
     *    Timer clock = PCLK1 = 170 MHz (APB1 prescaler = 1)
     *    PWM Frequency = 20 kHz -> Period = 170,000,000 / 20,000 = 8500 counts
     *    ARR = 8500 - 1 = 8499
     *    Duty cycle = 40% -> CCR1 = 8500 * 0.40 = 3400 counts
     */
    TIM3->PSC = 0;
    TIM3->ARR = 8499;
    TIM3->CCR1 = 3400;

    /* 4. Configure Channel 1: PWM Mode 1 (OC1M = 0110b), preload enable */
    TIM3->CCMR1 &= ~TIM_CCMR1_CC1S_Msk;                         /* Channel 1 as output */
    TIM3->CCMR1 |= (TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_1 | TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_2)        /* PWM mode 1 */
                |  TIM_CCMR1_OC1PE;                             /* Preload enable */

    /* 5. Enable output on CC1, active-high polarity (CC1P = 0) */
    TIM3->CCER |= TIM_CCER_CC1E;

    /* 6. Enable auto-reload preload and start counter */
    TIM3->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_ARPE;                                  /* Auto-reload preload enable */
    TIM3->EGR  = TIM_EGR_UG;                                    /* Generate update to latch PSC/ARR/CCR1 */
    TIM3->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_CEN;                                   /* Enable counter */
}
```

### Explanation
* **Clocks & Timing:** Because the APB1 prescaler is 1, the timer frequency is equal to PCLK1 ($170\text{ MHz}$). An ARR value of $8499$ with $\text{PSC} = 0$ gives an overflow period of $8500$ ticks, producing exactly $\frac{170\text{ MHz}}{8500} = 20\text{ kHz}$.
* **Duty Cycle:** In PWM mode 1 (upcounting), the output is active while $\text{CNT} < \text{CCR1}$. A $\text{CCR1}$ of $3400$ gives $\frac{3400}{8500} = 40\%$ active-high time.
* **Pin Routing:** PA6 is assigned to TIM3_CH1 via Alternate Function 2 (`AF2`).

### Hardware Conflict Note
TIM3 channels share a single 16-bit counter, prescaler (`PSC`), and auto-reload register (`ARR`). In edge-aligned PWM mode 1, **all channels on TIM3 must share the same PWM frequency**. 

Additionally, at 170 MHz, a 1 kHz period requires $170{,}000{,}000 / 1{,}000 = 170{,}000$ clock cycles, which exceeds the 16-bit limit of TIM3 (`ARR` max 65,535) and requires `PSC > 1`. Changing TIM3's prescaler and ARR to achieve 1 kHz will drop Channel 1 (the LED) from 20 kHz down to 1 kHz.

