### Solution A: Independent Timer on PA7 via TIM17_CH1 (Recommended)
To keep the status LED at 20 kHz on TIM3_CH1 and drive the buzzer at 1 kHz, PA7 is mapped to **TIM17_CH1 (AF1)**. TIM17 has its own independent timebase.

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void buzzer_tim17_init(void)
{
    /* 1. Enable GPIOA and TIM17 peripheral clocks */
    RCC->AHB2ENR |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN;
    RCC->APB2ENR |= RCC_APB2ENR_TIM17EN;

    /* 2. Configure PA7 as Alternate Function 1 (TIM17_CH1) */
    GPIOA->MODER   = (GPIOA->MODER & ~GPIO_MODER_MODE7_Msk)
                   | (0x2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE7_Pos);            /* AF mode (10b) */
    GPIOA->AFR[0]  = (GPIOA->AFR[0] & ~GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL7_Msk)
                   | (1U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL7_Pos);              /* AF1 = TIM17_CH1 */
    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (0x3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED7_Pos);

    /* 3. Configure TIM17 time base for 1 kHz PWM
     *    Timer clock = 170 MHz
     *    Prescaler = 169 -> f_cnt = 170 MHz / (169 + 1) = 1 MHz
     *    ARR = 1000 - 1 = 999 -> f_pwm = 1 MHz / 1000 = 1 kHz
     *    Duty cycle = 50% -> CCR1 = 500
     */
    TIM17->PSC  = 169;
    TIM17->ARR  = 999;
    TIM17->CCR1 = 500;

    /* 4. Configure Channel 1: PWM mode 1, preload enable */
    TIM17->CCMR1 &= ~TIM_CCMR1_CC1S_Msk;                        /* Output */
    TIM17->CCMR1 |= (TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_1 | TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_2)       /* PWM mode 1 */
                 |  TIM_CCMR1_OC1PE;                            /* Preload enable */

    /* 5. Enable output on Channel 1 */
    TIM17->CCER |= TIM_CCER_CC1E;

    /* 6. TIM17 is an advanced/break timer: Main Output Enable (MOE) is required */
    TIM17->BDTR |= TIM_BDTR_MOE;

    /* 7. Latch parameters and start counter */
    TIM17->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_ARPE;
    TIM17->EGR  = TIM_EGR_UG;
    TIM17->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_CEN;
}
```

