### Solution B: Strictly TIM3_CH2 (Forces Both Channels to 1 kHz)
If PA7 **must** use TIM3_CH2 (AF2), TIM3 must be reconfigured with a prescaler, forcing Channel 1 (LED) and Channel 2 (buzzer) to both run at 1 kHz:

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void buzzer_tim3_ch2_init(void)
{
    /* 1. Configure PA7 as Alternate Function 2 (TIM3_CH2) */
    GPIOA->MODER   = (GPIOA->MODER & ~GPIO_MODER_MODE7_Msk)
                   | (0x2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE7_Pos);
    GPIOA->AFR[0]  = (GPIOA->AFR[0] & ~GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL7_Msk)
                   | (2U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL7_Pos);              /* AF2 = TIM3_CH2 */
    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (0x3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED7_Pos);

    /* 2. Reconfigure TIM3 time base to 1 kHz for both channels:
     *    f_cnt = 170 MHz / (169 + 1) = 1 MHz
     *    ARR = 1000 - 1 = 999 (1 kHz)
     */
    TIM3->PSC  = 169;
    TIM3->ARR  = 999;

    /* Re-scale CH1 (LED) 40% duty cycle: 1000 * 0.40 = 400 */
    TIM3->CCR1 = 400;

    /* Configure CH2 (Buzzer) 50% duty cycle: 1000 * 0.50 = 500 */
    TIM3->CCR2 = 500;

    /* 3. Configure Channel 2: PWM mode 1, preload enable */
    TIM3->CCMR1 &= ~TIM_CCMR1_CC2S_Msk;                         /* CC2 as output */
    TIM3->CCMR1 |= (TIM_CCMR1_OC2M_1 | TIM_CCMR1_OC2M_2)       /* PWM mode 1 */
                |  TIM_CCMR1_OC2PE;                             /* Preload enable */

    /* 4. Enable CH2 output */
    TIM3->CCER |= TIM_CCER_CC2E;

    /* 5. Latch changes */
    TIM3->EGR = TIM_EGR_UG;
}
```

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void usart3_debug_init(void)
{
    /* 1. Enable GPIOB and USART3 peripheral clocks */
    RCC->AHB2ENR  |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOBEN;
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_USART3EN;

    /* 2. Configure PB10 (TX) and PB11 (RX) as Alternate Function 7 (USART3) */
    /* PB10 */
    GPIOB->MODER   = (GPIOB->MODER & ~GPIO_MODER_MODE10_Msk)
                   | (0x2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE10_Pos);          /* AF mode (10b) */
    GPIOB->AFR[1]  = (GPIOB->AFR[1] & ~GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL10_Msk)
                   | (7U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL10_Pos);            /* AF7 */
    GPIOB->OSPEEDR |= (0x3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED10_Pos);     /* High speed */

    /* PB11 */
    GPIOB->MODER   = (GPIOB->MODER & ~GPIO_MODER_MODE11_Msk)
                   | (0x2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE11_Pos);          /* AF mode (10b) */
    GPIOB->AFR[1]  = (GPIOB->AFR[1] & ~GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL11_Msk)
                   | (7U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL11_Pos);            /* AF7 */
    GPIOB->PUPDR   = (GPIOB->PUPDR & ~GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD11_Msk)
                   | (0x1U << GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD11_Pos);          /* Pull-up on RX */

    /* 3. Configure USART3 frame format while UE = 0:
     *    Default reset values already provide:
     *    - 8 data bits: M[1:0] = 00b (CR1: bit 28 = 0, bit 12 = 0)
     *    - Parity control disabled: PCE = 0 (CR1: bit 10 = 0)
     *    - Oversampling by 16: OVER8 = 0 (CR1: bit 15 = 0)
     *    - 1 stop bit: STOP[1:0] = 00b (CR2: bits [13:12] = 00b)
     */
    USART3->CR1 = 0;
    USART3->CR2 = 0;
    USART3->CR3 = 0;

    /* 4. Set baud rate before enabling the peripheral:
     *    f_CK = PCLK1 = 170 MHz (RCC_CCIPR reset value uses PCLK1 for USART3)
     *    With OVER8 = 0: USARTDIV = f_CK / Baud = 170,000,000 / 115,200 ≈ 1475.694
     *    BRR = round(170,000,000 / 115,200) = 1476 (0x05C4)
     *    Actual baud rate: 170,000,000 / 1476 ≈ 115,176.15 baud (-0.02% error)
     */
    USART3->BRR = 1476U;

    /* 5. Enable Transmitter, Receiver, and USART peripheral */
    USART3->CR1 |= USART_CR1_TE | USART_CR1_RE | USART_CR1_UE;
}
```

### Explanation
* **Clock Source & Baud Rate:** By reset default in `RCC->CCIPR`, USART3 clock selection (`USART3SEL[1:0]`) is `00` (PCLK1 = 170 MHz). For standard oversampling by 16 (`OVER8 = 0`), the baud rate divider register is directly $BRR = \text{round}\left(\frac{170{,}000{,}000}{115{,}200}\right) = 1476$ (`0x05C4`), yielding an error of only $-0.02\%$.
* **Sequencing:** The frame configuration (`CR1`, `CR2`, `CR3`) and `BRR` are loaded before setting the `UE` bit, strictly satisfying the requirement that the baud-rate register is written prior to peripheral enablement [RM0440 p.1387].
* **Pin Multiplexing:** PB10 and PB11 are mapped to `AF7` in `GPIOB->AFR[1]` (AFRH), corresponding to `USART3_TX` and `USART3_RX` respectively.

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

int main(void)
{
    /* =========================================================================
     * 1. Peripheral Clocks Enable
     * ========================================================================= */
    RCC->AHB2ENR  |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN | RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOBEN;
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_TIM3EN | RCC_APB1ENR1_USART3EN;
    RCC->APB2ENR  |= RCC_APB2ENR_TIM17EN;

    /* =========================================================================
     * 2. GPIO Configuration
     * ========================================================================= */
    /* PA6: AF2 (TIM3_CH1) - LED PWM */
    GPIOA->MODER   = (GPIOA->MODER & ~GPIO_MODER_MODE6_Msk)
                   | (0x2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE6_Pos);
    GPIOA->AFR[0]  = (GPIOA->AFR[0] & ~GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL6_Msk)
                   | (2U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL6_Pos);
    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (0x3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED6_Pos);

    /* PA7: AF1 (TIM17_CH1) - Buzzer PWM
     * Routed to TIM17_CH1 (AF1) because TIM3 cannot produce two different 
     * frequencies (20 kHz and 1 kHz) simultaneously on its shared counter. */
    GPIOA->MODER   = (GPIOA->MODER & ~GPIO_MODER_MODE7_Msk)
                   | (0x2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE7_Pos);
