### Bare-Metal C Implementation

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void tim1_pa8_pwm_init(void)
{
    /* 1. Enable peripheral clocks for GPIOA and TIM1 */
    RCC->AHB2ENR |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN;
    RCC->APB2ENR |= RCC_APB2ENR_TIM1EN;

    /* 2. Configure PA8 as Alternate Function (AF6 - TIM1_CH1) */
    /* Set MODER8 to Alternate Function mode (binary 10) */
    GPIOA->MODER &= ~GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Msk;
    GPIOA->MODER |= (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Pos);

    /* Set high speed for output pin */
    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED8_Pos);

    /* Configure Alternate Function AF6 on PA8 (AFRH / AFR[1], index 8 -> pin 8) */
    GPIOA->AFR[1] &= ~GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Msk;
    GPIOA->AFR[1] |= (6U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Pos);

    /* 3. Configure TIM1 timebase (170 MHz clock, 20 kHz PWM) */
    TIM1->PSC = 0U;            /* Timer clock prescaler: 170 MHz / 1 = 170 MHz */
    TIM1->ARR = 8500U - 1U;    /* 8499 -> 170 MHz / 8500 = 20 kHz */
    TIM1->CCR1 = 2125U;        /* 25% duty cycle: 8500 * 0.25 = 2125 */

    /* 4. Configure Channel 1 for PWM Mode 1 and enable preload */
    /* OC1M[3:0] = 0110b for PWM mode 1, OC1PE = 1 to enable preload */
    TIM1->CCMR1 &= ~TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_Msk;
    TIM1->CCMR1 |= (TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_1 | TIM_CCMR1_OC1M_2) | TIM_CCMR1_OC1PE;

    /* 5. Enable Channel 1 output, active-high polarity (CC1P = 0) */
    TIM1->CCER &= ~TIM_CCER_CC1P;
    TIM1->CCER |= TIM_CCER_CC1E;

    /* 6. Enable auto-reload preload (ARPE) and generate an update event to latch values */
    TIM1->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_ARPE;
    TIM1->EGR = TIM_EGR_UG;

    /* 7. Enable Main Output (MOE) in BDTR (required for advanced timer TIM1) */
    TIM1->BDTR |= TIM_BDTR_MOE;

    /* 8. Enable counter */
    TIM1->CR1 |= TIM_CR1_CEN;
}
```

### Explanation

- **Clocks**: `RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN` powers GPIO Port A, and `RCC_APB2ENR_TIM1EN` powers TIM1 [[STM32G474_RM0440 p.1265]].
- **GPIO Multiplexing**: PA8 alternate function 6 (`AF6`) is routed through `AFR[1]` (AFRH) bits [3:0] [[STM32G474_Datasheet p.62]].
- **PWM Output Mode 1**: Configured via `OC1M = 0110b` in `TIM1->CCMR1`. With upcounting, the output stays high while `TIM1_CNT < TIM1_CCR1` and goes low once the counter matches `TIM1_CCR1`, yielding an active-high 25% duty cycle pulse [[STM32G474_RM0440 p.1265]].
- **Break and Dead-Time Register (`BDTR`)**: Advanced timers (TIM1/TIM8/TIM20) gate their outputs via the `MOE` (Main Output Enable) bit. Setting `TIM1->BDTR |= TIM_BDTR_MOE` connects the compare output to the physical pad [[STM32G474_RM0440 p.1265]].

