---

#### Option B: Keep 170 MHz (Requires Boost Mode)
If your application strictly requires **170 MHz**, the internal regulator must remain in **Range 1 Boost mode** (`PWR->CR5 &= ~PWR_CR5_R1MODE;`), as shown in Message 1. Attempting 170 MHz with `R1MODE = 1` violates the operating conditions of the chip and causes erratic behavior or flash read faults due to insufficient internal core voltage ($V_{\text{CORE}}$).

