Per [STM32G474_RM0440 p.233] and [STM32G474_RM0440 p.280], switching from HSI16 to PLL at $f_{HCLK} > 80\text{ MHz}$ and into Boost Mode requires a transition state:
1. Ensure HSI16 is ready (`HSIRDY = 1`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.287].
2. Enable the Power interface clock (`RCC_APB1ENR1_PWREN = 1`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.309].
3. Set Flash latency to 4 wait states (`FLASH_ACR_LATENCY = 4`), and enable prefetch and caches [STM32G474_RM0440 p.98, p.130].
4. Set the AHB prescaler to divide by 2 (`HPRE = 1000b`) as the intermediate transition frequency [STM32G474_RM0440 p.233, p.280].
5. Switch the regulator to Range 1 Boost Mode by clearing `R1MODE` in `PWR_CR5` [STM32G474_RM0440 p.233, p.267].
6. Configure PLL parameters ($M=4, N=85, R=2$, PLLSRC = HSI16), enable the PLL (`PLLON = 1`), enable the R output (`PLLREN = 1`), and wait for `PLLRDY = 1` [STM32G474_RM0440 p.278, p.291].
7. Switch system clock to PLL (`SW = 11b`) and wait until confirmed by `SWS == 11b` [STM32G474_RM0440 p.279, p.289].
8. Wait for at least $1\ \mu\text{s}$ in the transition state before restoring the AHB prescaler [STM32G474_RM0440 p.233, p.280].
9. Clear the AHB prescaler back to divide by 1 (`HPRE = 0000b`) to bring HCLK to full 170 MHz [STM32G474_RM0440 p.233, p.290].

---

### 4. Implementation Code (`rcc_config_170mhz.c`)

