### 1. Hardware Constraints & SAADC Input Range

1. **Absolute Maximum & Operating Ratings**:
   - The recommended operating range for supply voltage $V_{DD}$ is $1.7\text{ V}$ (min), $3.0\text{ V}$ (typ), up to $3.6\text{ V}$ (max) [nRF52840_PS p.971].
   - For any I/O pin, when $V_{DD} \le 3.6\text{ V}$, the absolute maximum rating is $V_{I/O} \le V_{DD} + 0.3\text{ V}$ (and never below $-0.3\text{ V}$ or above $3.9\text{ V}$) [nRF52840_PS p.972].
   - Applying an unattenuated 5.0 V signal directly to an nRF52840 pin will forward-bias the internal ESD protection diodes and damage the device.
   - For analog inputs specifically: *“Inputs AIN0 to AIN7 cannot exceed $V_{DD}$ or be lower than $V_{SS}$”* [nRF52840_PS p.677].

2. **SAADC Reference & Gain**:
   - The nRF52840 SAADC features an internal bandgap reference $V_{\text{REF}} = 0.6\text{ V}$ [nRF52840_PS p.677].
