### 1. Pin Selection and Alternate Functions

For the **I2C3** controller peripheral on the STM32G474 (LQFP64 package [STM32G474_Datasheet p.65]), we allocate:
- **`PC8`** (pin 40): **`I2C3_SCL`**, Alternate Function 8 (**AF8**) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.75].
- **`PC9`** (pin 41): **`I2C3_SDA`**, Alternate Function 8 (**AF8**) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.75].

Both pins are 5 V tolerant (`FT_f` I/O structure) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.65] and belong to `GPIOC`, leaving `PA8` free for `TIM1_CH1`.

---

### 2. Voltage Domain & Level Shifting Notice

- The STM32G474 runs at $V_{\text{DD}} = 3.3\text{ V}$. For all I/O pins except FT_c, the datasheet specifies minimum input high voltage $V_{\text{IH(min)}} = 0.7 \times V_{\text{DD}} = 0.7 \times 3.3\text{ V} = 2.31\text{ V}$ [STM32G474_Datasheet p.128].
- The BME280 sensor operates with a $1.8\text{ V}$ I/O supply rail ($V_{\text{DDIO}} = 1.8\text{ V}$). A direct high level of $1.8\text{ V}$ is below $V_{\text{IH(min)}} = 2.31\text{ V}$ ($1.8\text{ V} < 2.31\text{ V}$), so the STM32 cannot reliably sample high levels from the sensor.
- **Hardware requirement**: An external bidirectional I2C level shifter (e.g. PCA9306 or dual N-channel MOSFET level translator) is required between the STM32G474 ($3.3\text{ V}$ domain) and the BME280 ($1.8\text{ V}$ domain).

---

### 3. Clock Source and TIMINGR Calculation

We select the internal **HSI16** ($16\text{ MHz}$) oscillator as the independent kernel clock for I2C3 by writing `0b10` to `I2C3SEL` in `RCC->CCIPR` [STM32G474_RM0440 p.322].

Following the reference timing configuration in Table 360 (*Timing settings for $f_{\text{I2CCLK}} = 16\text{ MHz}$, Standard-mode 100 kHz*) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1657]:
- **`PRESC`** = 3 ($0\text{x}3 \implies t_{\text{PRESC}} = (3 + 1) \times \frac{1}{16\text{ MHz}} = 250\text{ ns}$) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1681]
- **`SCLDEL`** = 4 ($0\text{x}4 \implies t_{\text{SCLDEL}} = (4 + 1) \times 250\text{ ns} = 1250\text{ ns}$) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1681]
- **`SDADEL`** = 2 ($0\text{x}2 \implies t_{\text{SDADEL}} = 2 \times 250\text{ ns} = 500\text{ ns}$) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1681]
- **`SCLH`** = 15 ($0\text{x}0\text{F} \implies t_{\text{SCLH}} = (15 + 1) \times 250\text{ ns} = 4.0\text{ µs}$) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1681]
- **`SCLL`** = 19 ($0\text{x}13 \implies t_{\text{SCLL}} = (19 + 1) \times 250\text{ ns} = 5.0\text{ µs}$) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1681]

Writing these bitfields directly to `I2C3->TIMINGR`:
`TIMINGR = (3U << 28) | (4U << 20) | (2U << 16) | (0x0FU << 8) | (0x13U << 0)`.

---

### 4. Bare-Metal C Implementation

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

void i2c3_controller_init(void) {
