* We select the standard $115200\text{ bps}$ baud rate used by typical ESP32 serial bridges.
* By default, USART2 clock source is $\text{PCLK1} = 170\text{ MHz}$.
* With oversampling by 16:
  $$\text{USARTDIV} = \frac{f_{\text{PCLK1}}}{\text{Baud}} = \frac{170\,000\,000}{115200} \approx 1475.694$$
