### Design Plan

#### 1. 3.3 V Power Budget and LDO Adequacy Check
* **STM32G474:** At 170 MHz in Range 1 Boost mode executing from Flash with peripherals active, typical current draw is approximately $35\text{--}45\text{ mA}$.
* **Pressure Sensor Module:** Specified at $1\text{ mA}$.
* **ESP32-WROOM:** Although average Wi-Fi operation requires $100\text{--}240\text{ mA}$, peak current during RF transmission bursts and calibration transients reaches $350\text{--}500\text{ mA}$.
* **Verdict:** The proposed **250 mA LDO is inadequate**. While adequate for the STM32 and sensor alone, the ESP32 will cause severe supply-voltage brownouts and reboots during Wi-Fi transmission. The regulator must be upgraded to one rated for at least **$500\text{ mA}$** (ideally $\ge 800\text{ mA}$) with low ESR bulk decoupling ($10\text{--}22\ \mu\text{F}$).

---

#### 2. Logic-Level Compatibility
* **STM32G474:** Operates at $V_{\text{DD}} = 3.3\text{ V}$.
* **Sensor Module:** $3.3\text{ V}$ I/O with integrated $4.7\text{ k}\Omega$ pull-up resistors to $3.3\text{ V}$.
* **ESP32-WROOM:** $3.3\text{ V}$ I/O.
* **Compatibility:** Both interfaces operate at the same nominal $3.3\text{ V}$ CMOS domain; voltage levels ($V_{\text{IH}}, V_{\text{IL}}, V_{\text{OH}}, V_{\text{OL}}$) are directly compatible without external level shifting.

---

#### 3. Pin Allocation
| Peripheral | Pin | Alternate Function | Mode / Configuration | Destination |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **OSC_IN / OUT** | PF0 / PF1 | — | Analog / HSE crystal oscillator | 8 MHz Crystal + Load Caps |
| **USART2_TX** | PA2 | AF7 | Alternate Function, Push-Pull, High Speed | ESP32 RXD0 / UART RX |
| **USART2_RX** | PA3 | AF7 | Alternate Function, Input Floating/Pull-up | ESP32 TXD0 / UART TX |
| **I2C1_SCL** | PB8 | AF4 | Alternate Function, Open-Drain | Pressure Sensor SCL |
| **I2C1_SDA** | PB9 | AF4 | Alternate Function, Open-Drain | Pressure Sensor SDA |

---

#### 4. Clock Tree Configuration (HSE to 170 MHz)
To achieve $170\text{ MHz}$ using an external $8\text{ MHz}$ crystal:
* **HSE:** $8\text{ MHz}$
* **PLL Prescaler ($M$):** $2 \implies f_{\text{VCO\_IN}} = \frac{8\text{ MHz}}{2} = 4\text{ MHz}$ (valid range: $4\text{--}16\text{ MHz}$).
* **PLL Multiplier ($N$):** $85 \implies f_{\text{VCO\_OUT}} = 4\text{ MHz} \times 85 = 340\text{ MHz}$ (valid range: $128\text{--}544\text{ MHz}$).
* **PLL Output Divider ($R$):** $2 \implies f_{\text{PLLCLK}} = \frac{340\text{ MHz}}{2} = 170\text{ MHz}$ (error: $0.00\%$).
* **System Prescalers:** $\text{AHB PRESC} = 1 \implies \text{HCLK} = 170\text{ MHz}$; $\text{APB1 PRESC} = 1 \implies \text{PCLK1} = 170\text{ MHz}$; $\text{APB2 PRESC} = 1 \implies \text{PCLK2} = 170\text{ MHz}$.
* **Power & Flash Configuration:**
  * For $f_{\text{SYSCLK}} > 150\text{ MHz}$, Range 1 Boost Mode is required (`PWR_CR5_R1MODE` cleared).
  * At $170\text{ MHz}$ in Boost Mode, Flash access latency requires **4 wait states** (`FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS`).

---

#### 5. Peripheral Timing Calculations
* **USART2 (Baud Rate Register):**
  * Target: $115200\text{ baud}$, oversampling by 16, clock source $\text{PCLK1} = 170\text{ MHz}$.
  * $\text{USARTDIV} = \frac{170\,000\,000}{115\,200} \approx 1475.694 \implies \text{USART2->BRR} = 1476\ (0\text{x}05\text{C}4)$.
  * Actual Baud Rate $= \frac{170\,000\,000}{1476} \approx 115\,176.15\text{ baud}$.
  * Error $= \frac{115176.15 - 115200}{115200} \times 100\% = -0.021\%$, well within the $\pm 2\%$ tolerance.
* **I2C1 (Standard Mode, 100 kHz):**
  * Clock Source: $\text{PCLK1} = 170\text{ MHz}$.
  * Prescaler $\text{PRESC} = 15$ ($0\text{xF}$) $\implies t_{\text{PRESC}} = \frac{15 + 1}{170\text{ MHz}} = 94.118\text{ ns}$.
  * Target period $= 10\ \mu\text{s} \implies \approx 106\ t_{\text{PRESC}}$ cycles:
    * $\text{SCLDEL} = 4 \implies t_{\text{SU;DAT}} = (4 + 1) \times 94.118\text{ ns} = 470.6\text{ ns} \ (> 250\text{ ns})$.
    * $\text{SDADEL} = 2 \implies t_{\text{HD;DAT}} = 2 \times 94.118\text{ ns} = 188.2\text{ ns} \ (> 0\text{ ns})$.
    * $\text{SCLH} = 51 \implies t_{\text{HIGH}} = (51 + 1) \times 94.118\text{ ns} = 4.894\ \mu\text{s} \ (> 4.0\ \mu\text{s})$.
    * $\text{SCLL} = 53 \implies t_{\text{LOW}} = (53 + 1) \times 94.118\text{ ns} = 5.082\ \mu\text{s} \ (> 4.7\ \mu\text{s})$.
    * $t_{\text{PERIOD}} \approx 9.976\ \mu\text{s} \implies f_{\text{SCL}} \approx 100.24\text{ kHz}$.
  * $\text{TIMINGR} = (15 \ll 28) \mid (4 \ll 20) \mid (2 \ll 16) \mid (51 \ll 8) \mid 53 = 0\text{xF0423335}$.

---

### Bare-Metal Initialization Code

```c
