### Design Plan

#### 1. Clock Tree Configuration (170 MHz)
* **Target Frequency:** $SYSCLK = HCLK = PCLK1 = PCLK2 = 170\text{ MHz}$.
* **HSE & PLL Setup:**
  * Source: $f_{HSE} = 16\text{ MHz}$.
  * PLL input: $f_{PLL,IN} = f_{HSE} / M = 16\text{ MHz} / 4 = 4\text{ MHz}$ (valid range: $4\text{ to } 16\text{ MHz}$).
  * VCO frequency: $f_{VCO} = f_{PLL,IN} \times N = 4\text{ MHz} \times 85 = 340\text{ MHz}$ (valid range: $64\text{ to } 344\text{ MHz}$).
  * Output frequency: $f_{PLL\_R} = f_{VCO} / R = 340\text{ MHz} / 2 = 170\text{ MHz}$.
  * Error: $0.0\%$.
* **Power & Flash Configuration:**
  * To operate at $170\text{ MHz}$, the core requires **Voltage Scaling Range 1 Boost Mode**.
  * Steps: Enable `PWR` clock; configure `PWR->CR1` for Range 1; clear `PWR_CR5_R1MODE` to switch to Boost Mode.
  * Flash Latency: At $170\text{ MHz}$ in Range 1 Boost mode, 4 wait states (4 WS) are required (`FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS`) [STM32G474 Reference Manual RM0440 p.96].

#### 2. Pin Allocation & Logic-Level Compatibility
* **Pin Allocation:**
  * **USART2:** PA2 = USART2_TX (AF7), PA3 = USART2_RX (AF7).
  * **I2C3:** PC8 = I2C3_SCL (AF8), PC9 = I2C3_SDA (AF8) (or PG7/PG8; PC8/PC9 selected).
* **Logic-Level Compatibility:**
  * **USART2 (STM32 to nRF52840 at $V_{DD} = 3.3\text{ V}$):**
    * Both devices run from $V_{DD} = 3.3\text{ V}$.
    * nRF52840: $V_{IH} \ge 0.7 \times V_{DD} = 2.31\text{ V}$, $V_{IL} \le 0.3 \times V_{DD} = 0.99\text{ V}$.
    * STM32G474: $V_{OH} \ge V_{DD} - 0.4\text{ V} = 2.9\text{ V}$, $V_{OL} \le 0.4\text{ V}$.
    * Fully direct-compatible without level shifters.
  * **I2C3 (STM32 to Sensor at $V_{DDIO} = 1.8\text{ V}$):**
    * Sensor I/O voltage is $1.8\text{ V}$. STM32G474 $V_{IH} = 0.49 \times V_{DD} + 0.26\text{ V} \approx 1.88\text{ V}$ (or $0.7 \times V_{DD} = 2.31\text{ V}$ for standard CMOS), which exceeds $1.8\text{ V}$.
    * STM32 cannot reliably sample an open-drain bus pulled up only to $1.8\text{ V}$ directly.
    * An active bi-directional I2C level translator (e.g., PCA9306 or Nexperia NTS0102) with high-side at $3.3\text{ V}$ and low-side at $1.8\text{ V}$ must be placed between the STM32 and the sensor.

#### 3. Low-Power Mode and Sleep-Current Budget
* **Mode Selection:**
  * **STM32G474:** **Stop 2 mode** preserves full SRAM and register contents while achieving sub-microamp consumption. RTC runs from LSE ($32.768\text{ kHz}$) to generate the 10-minute periodic wake-up event via RTC Wakeup Timer (`WUT`).
  * **nRF52840:** **System OFF** mode without RAM retention.
* **Sleep-Current Budget ($V_{DD} = 3.3\text{ V}$):**

| Component | Mode / Condition | Typical Current | Max Current |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **STM32G474** | Stop 2 Mode + RTC with LSE | $2.5\ \mu\text{A}$ | $4.5\ \mu\text{A}$ |
| **nRF52840** | System OFF (no RAM retention) | $0.4\ \mu\text{A}$ | $0.9\ \mu\text{A}$ |
| **Humidity Sensor** | Sleep state (powered via 1.8V LDO) | $1.0\ \mu\text{A}$ | $1.5\ \mu\text{A}$ |
| **1.8 V LDO Quiescent**| Ultra-low $I_Q$ LDO (e.g., TPS7A02) | $0.025\ \mu\text{A}$ | $0.1\ \mu\text{A}$ |
| **Level Shifter / Leakage**| Disabled / Idle open-drain lines | $0.1\ \mu\text{A}$ | $0.5\ \mu\text{A}$ |
| **Total Sleep Current** | **All components** | **$4.025\ \mu\text{A}$** | **$7.5\ \mu\text{A}$** |

*Result:* Fits strictly inside the $10\ \mu\text{A}$ budget.

#### 4. USART2 Configuration ($1\text{ Mbaud}$)
* Clock source: $PCLK1 = 170\text{ MHz}$.
* Oversampling by 16: $\text{OVER8} = 0$.
* Divider: $USARTDIV = f_{PCLK1} / \text{Baud} = 170\,000\,000 / 1\,000\,000 = 170 = \text{0x00AA}$.
* Error: $0.0\%$.

#### 5. I2C3 Configuration ($100\text{ kHz}$ Standard Mode)
* Clock source: $PCLK1 = 170\text{ MHz}$ ($t_{I2CCLK} \approx 5.882\text{ ns}$).
* Prescaler: $\text{PRESC} = 16 \implies t_{PRESC} = (16 + 1) \times 5.882\text{ ns} = 100\text{ ns}$.
* For $100\text{ kHz}$ Standard Mode ($t_{SCL} = 10\ \mu\text{s}$):
  * $t_{SCLL} = 5\ \mu\text{s} \implies \text{SCLL} = (5\ \mu\text{s} / 100\text{ ns}) - 1 = 49 = \text{0x31}$.
  * $t_{SCLH} = 5\ \mu\text{s} \implies \text{SCLH} = (5\ \mu\text{s} / 100\text{ ns}) - 1 = 49 = \text{0x31}$.
  * Data hold / setup: $\text{SDADEL} = 2$ ($200\text{ ns}$), $\text{SCLDEL} = 4$ ($400\text{ ns}$).
* Value for `I2C3->TIMINGR` = `0x00423131`.

---

### Bare-Metal C Code

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

int main(void)
{
    /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     * 1. Voltage Scaling Range 1 Boost Mode & Flash Latency Configuration
     * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_PWREN;

    /* Set Voltage Scaling Range 1 normal mode first */
    PWR->CR1 = (PWR->CR1 & ~PWR_CR1_VOS_Msk) | (1UL << PWR_CR1_VOS_Pos);

    /* Switch to Boost Mode: Clear R1MODE bit in PWR_CR5 */
    PWR->CR5 &= ~PWR_CR5_R1MODE;

    /* At 170 MHz in Range 1 Boost, 4 Wait States (WS) are required */
    FLASH->ACR = (FLASH->ACR & ~FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_Msk) | FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS;
    while ((FLASH->ACR & FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_Msk) != FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS);

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     * 2. HSE & Main PLL Setup (16 MHz HSE -> 170 MHz SYSCLK)
     * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /* Enable HSE and wait for ready */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_HSEON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_HSERDY));

    /* Disable Main PLL to configure it */
    RCC->CR &= ~RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY);

    /* PLL Configuration:
     * PLLSRC = HSE (16 MHz)
     * PLLM = 4   -> 16 MHz / 4 = 4 MHz (PLLM[3:0] = 3)
     * PLLN = 85  -> 4 MHz * 85 = 340 MHz (PLLN[6:0] = 85)
     * PLLR = 2   -> 340 MHz / 2 = 170 MHz (PLLR[1:0] = 0)
     */
    RCC->PLLCFGR = RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLSRC_HSE
                 | (3UL << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLM_Pos)
                 | (85UL << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLN_Pos)
                 | (0UL << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLR_Pos)
                 | RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLREN;

    /* Enable PLL and wait for lock */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY));

    /* Select PLL as SYSCLK (SW = 3) */
    RCC->CFGR = (RCC->CFGR & ~RCC_CFGR_SW_Msk) | RCC_CFGR_SW_PLL;
    while ((RCC->CFGR & RCC_CFGR_SWS_Msk) != RCC_CFGR_SWS_PLL);

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     * 3. GPIO Clocks & Pin Assignment
     *    PA2: USART2_TX (AF7)
     *    PA3: USART2_RX (AF7)
     *    PC8: I2C3_SCL  (AF8)
     *    PC9: I2C3_SDA  (AF8)
     * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    RCC->AHB2ENR |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN | RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOCEN;

    /* Configure PA2 and PA3: AF7, High Speed, No Pull */
    GPIOA->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE2_Msk | GPIO_MODER_MODE3_Msk);
    GPIOA->MODER |= (2UL << GPIO_MODER_MODE2_Pos) | (2UL << GPIO_MODER_MODE3_Pos);
    GPIOA->AFR[0] |= (7UL << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL2_Pos) | (7UL << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL3_Pos);
    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (3UL << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED2_Pos) | (3UL << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED3_Pos);

    /* Configure PC8 and PC9: AF8, Open-Drain, Pull-Up */
    GPIOC->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Msk | GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Msk);
    GPIOC->MODER |= (2UL << GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Pos) | (2UL << GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Pos);
    GPIOC->OTYPER |= GPIO_OTYPER_OT8 | GPIO_OTYPER_OT9;
    GPIOC->PUPDR &= ~(GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD8_Msk | GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD9_Msk);
    GPIOC->PUPDR |= (1UL << GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD8_Pos) | (1UL << GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD9_Pos);
    GPIOC->AFR[1] |= (8UL << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Pos) | (8UL << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL9_Pos);

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     * 4. USART2 Configuration (1 Mbaud, 8N1, Oversample by 16)
     * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /* Select PCLK1 as USART2 clock source (default) */
    RCC->CCIPR &= ~RCC_CCIPR_USART2SEL_Msk;
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_USART2EN;

    /* Baud rate = 170 MHz / 170 = 1 MBaud */
    USART2->CR1 = 0;
    USART2->BRR = 170;
    USART2->CR1 = USART_CR1_TE | USART_CR1_RE | USART_CR1_UE;

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
     * 5. I2C3 Configuration (100 kHz Standard Mode, Open-Drain)
     * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    /* Select PCLK1 as I2C3 clock source (default) */
    RCC->CCIPR &= ~RCC_CCIPR_I2C3SEL_Msk;
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_I2C3EN;

    /* Disable I2C3 before configuration */
    I2C3->CR1 &= ~I2C_CR1_PE;

    /* TIMINGR: PRESC = 0x0, SCLDEL = 0x4, SDADEL = 0x2, SCLH = 0x31, SCLL = 0x31
     * PRESC = 16 (0x10): (16+1) * (1/170MHz) = 100 ns t_presc
     * SCLL  = 49 (0x31) -> (49+1) * 100 ns = 5.0 us
     * SCLH  = 49 (0x31) -> (49+1) * 100 ns = 5.0 us
     */
    I2C3->TIMINGR = (16UL << I2C_TIMINGR_PRESC_Pos)
                  | (4UL  << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLDEL_Pos)
                  | (2UL  << I2C_TIMINGR_SDADEL_Pos)
                  | (49UL << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLH_Pos)
                  | (49UL << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLL_Pos);

    /* Enable I2C3 peripheral */
    I2C3->CR1 |= I2C_CR1_PE;

    /* Main Execution Loop */
    while (1)
    {
    }
}
```

