# Sensor Node Design Report

## 1. Clock Tree Configuration (170 MHz from 16 MHz HSE)
- **Oscillator**: 16 MHz external crystal on HSE.
- **Main PLL Parameters**:
  - Input: HSE = 16 MHz
  - Prescaler $M = 4 \implies f_{\text{VCO\_IN}} = 16\text{ MHz} / 4 = 4\text{ MHz}$ (compliant with 2.66 – 16 MHz PLL input range [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123]).
  - Multiplier $N = 85 \implies f_{\text{VCO}} = 4\text{ MHz} \times 85 = 340\text{ MHz}$ (compliant with 96 – 344 MHz Range 1 VCO limit [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123]).
  - Output Divider $R = 2 \implies f_{\text{PLL\_R}} = 340\text{ MHz} / 2 = 170\text{ MHz}$ (error = 0.00 %, within ±0.1 %).
- **Core and Bus Prescalers**:
  - `HPRE` = 1 $\implies$ HCLK = 170 MHz
  - `PPRE1` = 1 $\implies$ PCLK1 = 170 MHz
  - `PPRE2` = 1 $\implies$ PCLK2 = 170 MHz
- **Voltage Scaling & Flash Latency**:
  - To operate above 150 MHz up to 170 MHz, Range 1 Boost mode is mandatory: bit `R1MODE` in register `PWR_CR5` must be cleared to 0 (default is 1 after reset) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.267].
  - At 170 MHz in Range 1 Boost mode, Flash access requires 4 wait states (`FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS`, 5 CPU cycles) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.98].

---

## 2. Pin Allocation
- **USART2**:
  - `PA2` (AF7, AF_PP): `USART2_TX`
  - `PA3` (AF7, AF_IN): `USART2_RX`
- **I2C3**:
  - `PC8` (AF8, AF_OD): `I2C3_SCL`
  - `PC9` (AF8, AF_OD): `I2C3_SDA`
  - *Rationale*: PC8 and PC9 are adjacent pins on Port C, available in LQFP64, FT_f structure (5 V tolerant, fast mode capable) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.65, 75].

---

## 3. Logic-Level Compatibility Analysis

### A. STM32G474 (3.3 V) $\leftrightarrow$ nRF52840 (3.3 V) on USART2
Both chips share the same 3.3 V supply rail:
- **STM32G474 Output $\rightarrow$ nRF52840 Input (PA2 TX $\rightarrow$ RX)**:
  - STM32 $V_{OH} \ge 2.9\text{ V}$ vs nRF52840 $V_{IH} = 2.31\text{ V}$, difference is $2.9\text{ V} - 2.31\text{ V} = 0.59\text{ V}$ margin $\implies$ **PASS** [STM32G474_Datasheet p.130, nRF52840_PS p.370].
  - STM32 $V_{OL} \le 0.4\text{ V}$ vs nRF52840 $V_{IL} = 0.99\text{ V}$, difference is $0.99\text{ V} - 0.4\text{ V} = 0.59\text{ V}$ margin $\implies$ **PASS**.
  - Maximum input voltage on nRF52840 pin is 3.6 V, safely above 3.3 V.
- **nRF52840 Output $\rightarrow$ STM32G474 Input (TX $\rightarrow$ PA3 RX)**:
  - nRF52840 $V_{OH} \ge 2.9\text{ V}$ vs STM32 $V_{IH} = 2.31\text{ V}$ $\implies$ **PASS**.
  - nRF52840 $V_{OL} \le 0.4\text{ V}$ vs STM32 $V_{IL} = 0.99\text{ V}$ $\implies$ **PASS**.
  - Direct connection is 100 % compatible without level shifters.

### B. STM32G474 (3.3 V) $\leftrightarrow$ Humidity Sensor (1.8 V) on I2C3
- **Voltage Domain Mismatch**:
  - The sensor I/O rail is 1.8 V. Its maximum high-level output voltage is 1.8 V.
  - STM32G474 standard $V_{IH,\text{min}} = 0.7 \times 3.3\text{ V} = 2.31\text{ V}$ [STM32G474_Datasheet p.128].
  - Because $1.8\text{ V} < 2.31\text{ V}$, the STM32 cannot reliably sample logic high without voltage translation.
  - Pulling the open-drain lines up to 3.3 V would exceed the 1.8 V sensor's maximum input voltage rating.
- **Required Solution**:
  - A bidirectional I2C level translator (e.g. PCA9306) between 3.3 V and 1.8 V is required.

---

## 4. Low-Power Mode Selection and Sleep Power Budget

### Mode Selection
- **Target Low-Power Mode**: **Standby Mode with RTC** (or **Shutdown Mode with RTC**).
  - Stop modes on STM32G4 consume $\ge 190\ \mu\text{A}$ typ. [STM32G474_Datasheet p.102], exceeding the 10 µA budget.
  - **Standby Mode with RTC** (clocked by 32.768 kHz LSE):
    - At 3.0 V, typical consumption is $0.885\ \mu\text{A}$ ($885\text{ nA}$) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.104].
    - Wake-up every 10 minutes is achieved using the RTC Periodic Wakeup Timer (WUT).
  - **Shutdown Mode with RTC**:
    - Typical consumption is under $1\ \mu\text{A}$ (43 nA RTC disabled, under 300 nA with RTC) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.105].

### Sleep Current Table
| Component | Mode / State | Typ. Current ($25^\circ\text{C}$, 3.3 V) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **STM32G474** | Standby mode + RTC from LSE | $0.885\ \mu\text{A}$ |
| **nRF52840** | System OFF (no RAM retention) | $0.4\ \mu\text{A}$ |
| **Humidity Sensor** | Deep Sleep / Power Down | $1\ \mu\text{A}$ |

The total sleep current computed as $0.885\ \mu\text{A} + 0.4\ \mu\text{A} + 1\ \mu\text{A} = 2.285\ \mu\text{A}$ is well within the 10 µA budget.

---

## 5. Firmware Implementation (`main.c`)

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

int main(void)
{
    /* =========================================================================
     * 1. POWER AND CLOCK CONFIGURATION
     * Target: SYSCLK = HCLK = PCLK1 = PCLK2 = 170 MHz from 16 MHz HSE
     * ========================================================================= */
    /* Enable Power Controller clock */
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_PWREN;

    /* To run at 170 MHz (> 150 MHz), Range 1 Boost mode is required.
     * Clear R1MODE bit in PWR_CR5 (0: Boost mode, 1: Normal mode). */
    PWR->CR5 &= ~PWR_CR5_R1MODE;

    /* At 170 MHz in Range 1 Boost mode, 4 Flash wait states are required (5 CPU cycles). */
    FLASH->ACR = (FLASH->ACR & ~FLASH_ACR_LATENCY) | FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS;
    while ((FLASH->ACR & FLASH_ACR_LATENCY) != FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS);

    /* Enable HSE oscillator (16 MHz external crystal) */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_HSEON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_HSERDY));

    /* Configure PLL:
     * Source: HSE (16 MHz)
     * PLLM = 4 (value 3 in PLLM[3:0]) -> f_VCO_IN = 16 MHz / 4 = 4 MHz
     * PLLN = 85 (value 85 in PLLN[6:0]) -> f_VCO = 4 MHz * 85 = 340 MHz
     * PLLR = 2 (value 0 in PLLR[1:0]) -> f_PLL_R = 340 MHz / 2 = 170 MHz
     * Enable PLLR output */
    RCC->PLLCFGR = RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLSRC_HSE |
                   (3U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLM_Pos) |
                   (85U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLN_Pos) |
                   (0U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLR_Pos) |
                   RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLREN;

    /* Enable PLL and wait for PLL lock */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY));

    /* Select PLL as SYSCLK */
    RCC->CFGR = (RCC->CFGR & ~RCC_CFGR_SW) | RCC_CFGR_SW_PLL;
    while ((RCC->CFGR & RCC_CFGR_SWS) != RCC_CFGR_SWS_PLL);

    /* =========================================================================
     * 2. PERIPHERAL CLOCK GATING
     * ========================================================================= */
    RCC->AHB2ENR |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN | RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOCEN;
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_USART2EN | RCC_APB1ENR1_I2C3EN;

    /* =========================================================================
     * 3. GPIO PIN CONFIGURATION
     * USART2: PA2 (TX, AF7), PA3 (RX, AF7)
     * I2C3:   PC8 (SCL, AF8), PC9 (SDA, AF8)
     * ========================================================================= */
    /* Configure PA2 and PA3 as Alternate Function 7 */
    GPIOA->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE2_Msk | GPIO_MODER_MODE3_Msk);
    GPIOA->MODER |= (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE2_Pos) | (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE3_Pos);
    GPIOA->AFR[0] &= ~((0xFU << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL2_Pos) | (0xFU << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL3_Pos));
    GPIOA->AFR[0] |= (7U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL2_Pos) | (7U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL3_Pos);
    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED2_Pos) | (3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED3_Pos);

    /* Configure PC8 and PC9 as Alternate Function 8, Open-Drain */
    GPIOC->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Msk | GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Msk);
    GPIOC->MODER |= (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Pos) | (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Pos);
    GPIOC->OTYPER |= GPIO_OTYPER_OT8 | GPIO_OTYPER_OT9; /* Open-drain */
    GPIOC->AFR[1] &= ~((0xFU << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Pos) | (0xFU << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL9_Pos));
    GPIOC->AFR[1] |= (8U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Pos) | (8U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL9_Pos);

    /* =========================================================================
     * 4. USART2 CONFIGURATION
     * Baud rate: 1 Mbaud, 8N1, 16x oversampling, f_CK = PCLK1 = 170 MHz
     * BRR = f_CK / Baud = 170000000 / 1000000 = 170
     * ========================================================================= */
    USART2->CR1 &= ~USART_CR1_UE;
    USART2->BRR = 170U;
    USART2->CR1 = USART_CR1_TE | USART_CR1_RE | USART_CR1_UE;

    /* =========================================================================
     * 5. I2C3 CONFIGURATION (Standard Mode 100 kHz)
     * Clock: PCLK1 = 170 MHz
     * TIMINGR: PRESC = 3 (div 4 -> t_I2CCLK = 23.53 ns)
     * SCLDEL = 4, SDADEL = 2, SCLH = 0xD8 (216), SCLL = 0xCE (206)
     * Total period ~ 10 us (100 kHz)
     * ========================================================================= */
    I2C3->CR1 &= ~I2C_CR1_PE;
    I2C3->TIMINGR = (3U << I2C_TIMINGR_PRESC_Pos) |
                    (4U << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLDEL_Pos) |
                    (2U << I2C_TIMINGR_SDADEL_Pos) |
                    (0xD8U << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLH_Pos) |
                    (0xCEU << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLL_Pos);
    I2C3->CR1 |= I2C_CR1_PE;

    /* Main loop */
    while (1)
    {
    }
}
